# oleskostudio.com — domains and publish

Site is already on production custom domains. Do not re-add them. Do not use Quick Connect (it would take over DNS). Do not move nameservers off Cloudflare. Do not touch Google MX or SPF.

## Live

- Default: `https://oleskostudio.com`
- www redirects to apex
- Staging: `https://olesko-website----development.webflow.io`
- Site ID: `6a7b43a328ec101a40bb1d20`
- Short name: `olesko-website----development`

## DNS (Cloudflare, proxy off / grey cloud)

- `A` `@` → `198.202.211.1`
- `CNAME` `www` → `cdn.webflow.com`
- `TXT` `_webflow` → `one-time-verification=1f42e90e-1d0f-4ffb-8b10-e92dc5088fb4`
- Never use `75.2.*` / `99.83.*` or `proxy-ssl.webflow.com`

## Publish

Webflow MCP cannot add custom domains (`list_sites` / `get_site` / `publish_site` only). Adding domains is dashboard UI: Manually add domain. Custom domains need a paid Site plan.

`publish_site` needs domain **IDs**, not hostnames. Do not publish unless Sebastian asks.

```json
{
  "site_id": "6a7b43a328ec101a40bb1d20",
  "customDomains": [
    "6a874109e067f5d3b357ad46",
    "6a874109e067f5d3b357ad4d"
  ],
  "publishToWebflowSubdomain": true
}
```

- `oleskostudio.com` → `6a874109e067f5d3b357ad46`
- `www.oleskostudio.com` → `6a874109e067f5d3b357ad4d`

Default domain is apex. After any default-domain change, publish for it to take effect.

